NAME
    m - bootstrap the technical m runtime and dispatch integrated commands

SYNOPSIS
    m
    m <command> [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    m resolves the technical runtime root, initializes the relocatable m
    runtime environment, exposes technical command paths, loads the core shell
    facilities, establishes the current state/resource roots and applies the
    environment projections of currently resolvable system facility defaults.

    With no command operand, m starts the managed shell through the shell
    facility.

    With a command operand, m resolves that command through the active command
    path, exports its resolved pathname as m_COMMAND_BIN, removes the command
    operand from the argument vector and executes the command body inside the
    initialized m runtime.

    Before dispatch or shell entry, facility-default provider environment is
    recomputed from authoritative provider selection and installed projection
    metadata. A valid ext-osarch selector chooses the active platform class;
    otherwise only generic provider classes can contribute environment.
    Facilities are applied in LC_ALL=C name order and later facilities win when
    they export the same variable. PATH is never supplied by facility-env;
    provider commands are exposed through the existing ext-osarch/ext PATH roots.

    Changes to facility defaults or provider package defaults are observed by
    later m bootstraps. Already-running parent processes and shells are not
    mutated retroactively. Invalid provider environment projection is reported
    without making the technical bootstrap unavailable.

    The bootstrap refuses to dispatch itself recursively as a command.

RUNTIME FUNCTIONS
    loadlib <library-reference>
        Load exactly one m-owned POSIX-shell library reference relative to
        m_LIB_DIR. The reference omits the final .lib.sh suffix.

        The resolved file must be a readable regular file and is sourced in the
        current shell environment.

        Return status:
            loaded library status
                returned unchanged after a successful load
            1   invalid invocation; exactly one reference is required
            2   resolved library file is missing, not regular, or unreadable

    loadsyslib <system-shell-library-reference>
        Load exactly one m system shell library below lib/sys/sh by delegating
        to loadlib with the sys/sh/ prefix.

        Examples:

            loadsyslib "array"
            loadsyslib "pkg/pkg-install"
            loadsyslib "rsudo/rsudo-mod-fs"

        Positional-parameter forwarding is not part of the loading interface.
        m- and RumiAI-owned shell code uses loadsyslib for owned lib/sys/sh
        dependencies; runtime/external pathname sourcing remains ordinary
        POSIX dot-sourcing.

        Return status:
            delegated loadlib/library status

EXIT STATUS
    With a dispatched command, m returns that command's status.
    Bootstrap, root-resolution or command-resolution failures return non-zero.

